      <slug></slug>
      <title>Low latency in Gervill and JavaSound</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Free Java devroom</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The shortcomings of JavaSound and a proposal for how to fix it.&lt;/p&gt;      </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Currently it is not easy or even possible with the current JavaSound API to write low-latency audio application without resorting to using external libraries. Also JavaSound doesn&amp;#39;t readily support 5.1/Surround or HD audio. I want to talk about those shortcomings of JavaSound and give a proposal on how to fix it.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I also want to make a demonstration of low-latency in Gervill.&lt;/p&gt;      </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="1761">Karl Helgason</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>